        <div class="section" id="presentation">
            <h2><span class="section-icon">📋</span>1. Overview</h2>
<p>NRJXpert brings six tools together in one application:</p>
<table>
<tr><th>Tool</th><th>Purpose</th><th>How to open</th></tr>
<tr><td><b>Network simulation</b></td><td>Draw a diagram (full or one-line), compute currents and voltages of a linear DC or AC network, run a load flow on a power system, short-circuit currents (IEC 60909); distributed-energy-resource and smart-grid studies: distribution load flow, time series, PV hosting capacity, dynamics, OPF and microgrid economic dispatch.</td><td>Main window</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Site weather data</b></td><td>Download solar irradiation, temperature and wind for any site (NASA POWER, PVGIS, Open-Meteo) and compute monthly averages.</td><td>Tools › Site weather data (<kbd>Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+M</kbd>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Photovoltaic systems</b></td><td>Sizing of centralised and decentralised stand-alone systems, costs, simulation versus the number of buildings, economic viability study (stand-alone or grid-connected).</td><td>Tools › Photovoltaic systems (<kbd>Cmd/Ctrl+P</kbd>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Wind systems</b></td><td>Statistical wind analysis (Weibull distribution), wind turbine output, number of machines for a given demand, economic viability study.</td><td>Tools › Wind systems (<kbd>Cmd/Ctrl+Shift+E</kbd>)</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Solar pumping</b></td><td>Sizing and simulation of a photovoltaic pumping system (direct-coupled or with battery): water needs, pump, PV array and tank, economic viability study.</td><td>“Solar pumping…” button of the Photovoltaic systems window, or the Renewables menu</td></tr>
<tr><td><b>Smart grid</b></td><td>SGAM architecture (layers, domains, zones, IEC 62559 use cases), CIM / CGMES network model import and export, remote-control point list, cybersecurity risk analysis (IEC 62443).</td><td>Tools menu</td></tr>
</table>
