        <div class="section" id="installation">
            <h2><span class="section-icon">💻</span>2. Installation and start-up</h2>
<h3>SimElecNetwork calculation server</h3>
<p>The calculation server is <b>supplied with the software and runs on your computer</b>: there is nothing else to install. NRJXpert starts it
automatically in the background at the first calculation and stops it when it closes. It can only be reached from your own computer and only
accepts requests from the application that started it.</p>
<ul>
<li><b>Default mode</b>: the « Use the local server on this computer » option (<b>Simulation › Calculation and server settings</b>) is ticked
from the installation: there is nothing to set up. While it is ticked, the address, port and access key are not used.</li>
<li><b>Offline operation</b>: calculations (linear network, load flow, short circuit, DER studies) run without an Internet connection.
The Internet is only used to activate the licence, for its periodic checks and to fetch online weather data (NASA POWER, PVGIS, Open-Meteo).</li>
<li><b>Time</b>: usual calculations take less than one second; DER studies (dynamics, OPF, economic dispatch) a few seconds.
The first calculation of a session takes a few seconds more, while the server starts.</li>
<li><b>Confidentiality</b>: diagrams and results never leave your computer. Only the licence communicates with the supplier
(licence identifier and a non-reversible fingerprint of the computer).</li>
<li><b>Log</b>: in case of trouble, the file <code>~/.nrjxpert/logs/server.log</code> (on Windows:
<code>%USERPROFILE%\.nrjxpert\logs\server.log</code>) keeps the server trace.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="licence">Licence and activation</h3>
<p>NRJXpert is used with a licence supplied by Niitan, according to the category: student, institution or professional. After the purchase you receive
an <b>activation key</b> by e-mail, of the form <code>NRJX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX-XXXXX</code>.
The licence is tied to your computer by an <b>online activation</b>, mandatory for all categories; it is managed by the local server. Without a licence, the software runs in
<b>demonstration mode</b>: the size of the diagrams is limited.</p>
<ol class="steps">
<li><div class="step-content">Open <b>Help › License…</b> and enter your activation key in the field provided (simplest: copy and paste it from the e-mail; upper or lower case and hyphens do not matter).</div></li>
<li><div class="step-content">Click <b>Activate</b> (Internet connection required). The status becomes « Active »; the window shows the category,
the holder, the expiry date and the next online check.</div></li>
</ol>
<ul>
<li><b>Periodic checks</b>: from time to time the software confirms the licence with the activation server, in the background when the Internet is
available. It warns before the deadline; after a short tolerance period without a check, the licence is suspended
(« Suspended — online check required ») and resumes as soon as a check succeeds.</li>
<li><b>Changing computer</b>: on the old computer, click <b>Release this computer</b>, then activate the licence on the new one. The number of
computers depends on the licence.</li>
<li><b>Power of PV and wind systems</b>: the Photovoltaic systems, Photovoltaic pumping and Wind systems modules, as well as the simulation of the Renewable energy blocks, calculate installations up to <b>1 MW</b> with the Student licence, <b>10 MW</b> with the Institution licence and up to <b>10 kW</b> in demonstration mode (PV peak power and installed wind power). The Professional / Expert licence has no such limit.</li>
<li><b>Transformer taps</b>: the tap changer (fixed or automatic) is available with every licence, demonstration mode included.</li>
<li><b>Reactive power compensation</b>: the switched shunt compensator is available with every licence, demonstration mode included; static var compensators (STATCOM, SVC) require an activated licence.</li>
<li><b>Renewal</b>: when your subscription is renewed with Niitan, the new expiry date is picked up automatically at the next online check (or immediately with <b>Check online</b>): no new key is needed.</li>
<li><b>Keep the key confidential</b>: do not share it; it is valid only for the number of computers of your licence. If it is lost or compromised, contact Niitan: a new key is sent to you and the old one stops working.</li>
<li><b>Licence notice</b>: the category (for example « Educational licence — non-commercial use ») is shown in the status bar.</li>
<li><b>Computer ID</b>: shown in the Licence window; give it to the support in case of an activation problem.</li>
</ul>

<!-- ====================================================================== -->
