        <div class="section" id="fichiers">
            <h2><span class="section-icon">📁</span>11. Files and folders</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>File / folder</th><th>Content</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>*.nxp</code></td><td>Network project (diagram, parameters, groups).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>*.nxpv</code></td><td>Photovoltaic project (site, demand, options, viability, imported weather data).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>*.nxeol</code></td><td>Wind project (site, measurements, turbine, production, viability).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>*.EOL</code></td><td>Old EolXpert projects (import only).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>~/.nrjxpert/pv/</code></td><td>Modified PV equipment databases (CSV).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>~/.nrjxpert/meteo/cache/</code></td><td>Weather service answers (90 days).</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>~/.nrjxpert/aide/</code></td><td>Copy of this guide, opened in the browser.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Figure and table exports</td><td><b>Right-click</b> any chart: PNG image (high resolution, white background), CSV data, copy the image or the data (paste into Excel). Right-click any table: CSV export (visible columns, all rows) or copy for Excel. CSV is UTF-8; ";" separator and decimal comma in French, "," and decimal point in English.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Exports</td><td>Monthly averages (CSV, “;” separator, decimal comma), sensitivities (CSV), reports (text).</td></tr>
</table>

<!-- ====================================================================== -->
            <a href="#top" class="back-to-top">↑ Back to top</a>
        </div>
        <div class="section" id="depannage">
            <h2><span class="section-icon">🛠️</span>12. Troubleshooting</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause and solution</th></tr>
<tr><td>The calculation does not start, « local server not found » or « the local server stopped »</td><td>Check that « Use the local server on this computer »
is ticked (default setting; Simulation › Calculation and server settings) and that the application is complete (the « server » folder must stay next to the application).
An antivirus or a firewall can block the start: allow NRJXpert and its calculation server. The file <code>~/.nrjxpert/logs/server.log</code> gives the cause.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Licence « missing », « not activated on this computer », « suspended » or « expired »</td><td>Open Help › License…: enter your activation key and click « Activate » (or « Check online » if the computer is already activated) (Internet connection required; the firewall must allow access to activation.nrjxpert.com over HTTPS). An expired licence is renewed with Niitan.</td></tr>
<tr><td>« Invalid » or « unknown activation key »</td><td>Check what you typed (copy and paste recommended; the key starts with NRJX and has four groups of five characters). If the message persists, contact Niitan with the e-mail address used for the purchase.</td></tr>
<tr><td>« Number of computers reached » or change of computer</td><td>On the old computer, use « Release this computer » in Help › License…, then activate on the new one.
If the old computer is no longer available, contact the support with the computer ID.</td></tr>
<tr><td>« server busy » or « maximum calculation time exceeded »</td><td>Many simultaneous calculations: try again in a moment. Study too heavy (long dynamics,
OPF over many steps, test bench with long tests): reduce the simulated duration, the number of steps or the length of the profiles.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Response time-out</td><td>Slow connection or long DER study (dynamics, OPF): reduce the simulated duration or the number of steps, then run again.</td></tr>
<tr><td>« The load flow needs a slack bus »</td><td>Place one generator bus of slack type.</td></tr>
<tr><td>« The network contains no source »</td><td>Add a source or a generator bus.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mixing of DC and AC sources refused</td><td>Calculate the DC and AC parts separately.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Weather download impossible</td><td>Internet connection or proxy; service temporarily unavailable (automatic retry); try again later or change the source.</td></tr>
<tr><td>December without irradiation (NASA)</td><td>CERES data are published a few months late: choose an earlier period.</td></tr>
<tr><td>PV: months in deficit</td><td>Size on the least sunny month, increase the tilt or the peak power.</td></tr>
<tr><td>PV: high-voltage module on a 12/24 V bus</td><td>Tick « MPPT charge controller ».</td></tr>
<tr><td>Wind: Weibull / series difference &gt; 10 %</td><td>Rounded measurements, many calms or bimodal distribution: the value calculated on the series is the most reliable.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Short circuit: « Configuration error of the short-circuit point »</td><td>Double-click on a terminal or place a fault on a line, then choose the « Short circuit » calculation.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Short circuit: « zero positive-sequence impedance »</td><td>A conventional generator without Rd, Xd is at the fault point: enter its impedances (inverters are current sources).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Short circuit: zero earth current</td><td>No zero-sequence path (isolated neutrals, delta winding): this is normal; otherwise enter R0, X0 and the neutral of the generators.</td></tr>
<tr><td>DER study refused: « non-radial network »</td><td>The distribution load flow needs a radial network: open a loop.</td></tr>
<tr><td>DER study: wrong profile length</td><td>All profiles and hourly prices must have the same number of values (DER study settings › Profiles).</td></tr>
<tr><td>Study (OPF, economic dispatch, test bench): server error</td><td>Run the calculation again. If the error persists, attach the file <code>~/.nrjxpert/logs/server.log</code> to your support request.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Test bench: « point of common coupling not found » or « does not separate an island »</td><td>Choose as PCC the switching device or series element located
between the slack bus (upstream grid, dynamic model « grid ») and the site, in the « Microgrid tests » tab.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Test bench: all dynamic tests fail (« collapse »)</td><td>No grid-forming source in the island: give a battery the grid-forming model (droop or VSM) or add a genset.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Help not opened</td><td>Open <code>~/.nrjxpert/aide/help-en.html</code> in a web browser.</td></tr>
</table>

