        <div class="section" id="glossaire">
            <h2><span class="section-icon">📚</span>13. Glossary and references</h2>
<div class="kv">
<b>Slack bus</b><span>Bus whose voltage and angle are imposed; it supplies the balance of power.</span>
<b>PV / PQ bus</b><span>Generator bus with P and V imposed / load bus with P and Q imposed.</span>
<b>Kt</b><span>Clearness index: ratio of ground irradiation to extraterrestrial irradiation.</span>
<b>NOCT</b><span>Cell temperature under 800 W/m², 20 °C, wind 1 m/s.</span>
<b>PR</b><span>Performance ratio: AC energy / (peak power × irradiation on the plane).</span>
<b>MPPT / PWM</b><span>Charge controller with maximum power point tracking / with simple switching.</span>
<b>DoD</b><span>Admissible depth of discharge of the battery.</span>
<b>Capacity factor</b><span>Energy produced / (rated power × 8760 h).</span>
<b>LCOE</b><span>Levelized cost of energy.</span>
<b>NPV, IRR</b><span>Net present value, internal rate of return.</span>
<b>DER</b><span>Distributed energy resources: generation (PV, wind, gensets) and storage connected to the distribution network.</span>
<b>I"k, ip</b><span>Initial symmetrical short-circuit current, peak current.</span>
<b>I_skPF</b><span>Short-circuit current of an inverter-based generator (« full converter »), limited by its control.</span>
<b>Grid-following / grid-forming inverter (GFL / GFM)</b><span>Inverter that follows the grid voltage (PLL) / that imposes its own voltage and frequency (droop, virtual synchronous machine VSM).</span>
<b>SOC</b><span>Battery state of charge.</span>
<b>RoCoF, nadir</b><span>Rate of change of frequency, minimum frequency after a disturbance.</span>
<b>OPF, MILP</b><span>Optimal power flow; mixed-integer linear programming.</span>
<b>SGAM</b><span>Smart Grid Architecture Model (IEC SRD 63200): domains × zones × interoperability layers.</span>
<b>ADMS, DERMS, VPP</b><span>Advanced distribution management system; DER management system; virtual power plant.</span>
<b>FLISR (FDIR)</b><span>Fault location, isolation and service restoration (self-healing).</span>
<b>FPI</b><span>Fault passage indicator.</span>
<b>SAIDI, SAIFI, MAIFI, ENS</b><span>Average interruption duration and frequency per customer; momentary interruptions; energy not supplied.</span>
<b>IVVC, IVVC/r, CVR</b><span>Integrated Volt/VAR control (with inverters); conservation voltage reduction.</span>
<b>V1G, V2G</b><span>Smart charging; bidirectional charging (vehicle-to-grid).</span>
<b>CIM</b><span>Common Information Model: IEC 61970 (transmission), IEC 61968 (distribution), IEC 62325 (markets).</span>
<b>PCC</b><span>Point of common coupling between the microgrid and the upstream grid.</span>
<b>AMI, HES, OBIS</b><span>Advanced metering infrastructure; head-end system; object identification system of DLMS/COSEM data.</span>
<b>NTL</b><span>Non-technical losses (theft, faulty meters, unregistered customers, billing errors).</span>
<b>VTN, VEN</b><span>Virtual top node (operator, aggregator) and virtual end node (site, VPP) of OpenADR.</span>
<b>SL-T, SL-A, FR</b><span>Target and achieved security levels, foundational requirements of IEC 62443.</span>
</div>
<h3>References</h3>
<ul class="small">
<li>Smart grids, standards: IEC SRD 63200 (SGAM), IEEE 2030.7 / 2030.8 (microgrids), IEEE 1547-2018, EN 50549, IEEE 1366 (reliability indices), IEEE P2030.14 (VPP), IEC 61970 / 61968 (CIM), IEC 61850, IEC 62056 (DLMS/COSEM), ITU-T G.9903 (G3-PLC), IEC 60870-5-104, ISO 15118, OCPP 2.0.1, OpenADR 2.0b, IEC 62559-2 (use cases), IEC 62443 and IEC 62351 (cybersecurity).</li>
<li>L. Thiaw: smart grid specialisation guide, École Supérieure Polytechnique (ESP), Université Cheikh Anta Diop de Dakar (UCAD), 2026.</li>
<li>J. A. Duffie, W. A. Beckman, <i>Solar Engineering of Thermal Processes</i>, Wiley (solar geometry, Liu-Jordan, Klein).</li>
<li>D. G. Erbs, S. A. Klein, J. A. Duffie, “Estimation of the diffuse radiation fraction…”, <i>Solar Energy</i> 28, 1982.</li>
<li>IEC 61400-12-1, power performance measurements of wind turbines; J. F. Manwell et al., <i>Wind Energy Explained</i>, Wiley.</li>
<li>C. G. Justus et al., “Methods for estimating wind speed frequency distributions”, <i>J. Appl. Meteorol.</i>, 1978.</li>
<li>IEC 60909-0:2016, Short-circuit currents in three-phase a.c. systems — Calculation of currents.</li>
<li>IEEE 1547-2018, interconnection of distributed energy resources (Q(V), P(V) controls).</li>
<li>NASA POWER: power.larc.nasa.gov; PVGIS: re.jrc.ec.europa.eu; Open-Meteo: open-meteo.com.</li>
<li>L. Thiaw: NRJXpert, EolXpert (C++, 2002) and PV Systems Analyser (MATLAB, 2010-2013) programs.</li>
<li>L. Thiaw: applied electricity course materials, École Supérieure Polytechnique (ESP), Université Cheikh Anta Diop de Dakar (UCAD).</li>
<li>L. Thiaw: SimElecNetwork, first development phase, 2018-2020, École Supérieure Polytechnique (ESP), Université Cheikh Anta Diop de Dakar (UCAD).</li>
</ul>
<p class="small">NRJXpert — ESP / UCAD, Dakar. This guide is copied to <code>~/.nrjxpert/aide/</code> each time it is opened from the Help menu.</p>
